{"file":"commands/release/capability.rs","line":537,"quote":"if !matches!(observed, Ok(ProviderObservationV1::Exact { .. })) { return Ok(None); }","class":"SUSPECT","what_is_lost":"Any Err from observe() (real GraphError, not only an unreachable registry), plus the recorded_repository() None at :540 (swallows .ok() at npm.rs:112/121/122, cargo.rs:42/51/52, registry.rs:309)","consequence":"The 'name taken by a different repository' pre-publish check silently reports clean when the registry or tool failed. The comment says it is advisory and the publish itself reports failures.","fix":"Count and report 'N name checks could not be made' as a diagnostic; only swallow the Indeterminate cause, propagate other errors"}
{"file":"tags.rs","line":283,"quote":".unwrap_or(true);  // may_have_held_name_at(...)","class":"SUSPECT","what_is_lost":"Git or history-read error while deciding whether a bare-named tag belongs to this package","consequence":"The tag is accepted as the package's last release, so the wrong base for the next version or changelog is possible. The comment says 'History that cannot be read is no evidence of another owner'. The same pattern is at lib.rs:322. Both fail towards 'keep the tag', and no diagnostic is emitted.","fix":"Push a Diagnostic (warning) when the history read errors, or propagate the error"}
{"file":"history.rs","line":99","quote":"read_identity(format, &text, &path).ok().and_then(|identity| identity.name)","class":"SUSPECT","what_is_lost":"Parse error of a historical manifest (also :132)","consequence":"A manifest that failed to parse at a past rev 'names nobody', which changes tag-ownership attribution. The comment says this is intended. A parse failure of our own history data is dropped uncounted.","fix":"Count the unparsable manifests and surface them via the diagnostics that tags.rs already collects"}
{"file":"commands/release/version_commit.rs","line":224,"quote":".ok().flatten(),  // read_effective_version(...)","class":"SUSPECT","what_is_lost":"ManifestError (parse error, or a workspace-inheritance read error) when reading the version at a commit","consequence":"effective_version_at returns None. That is documented ('does not parse ... gives None'). It is mixed in the same function as the carefully held git_failure, so a real ManifestError from the workspace-read closure is dropped too. The effect is that the 'moved past version commit' check can mis-answer.","fix":"Propagate non-parse ManifestErrors; only map parse failures to None"}
{"file":"napi.rs","line":72,"quote":"read_napi_targets(&pkg_json_path, &val).ok().flatten()","class":"SUSPECT","what_is_lost":"Malformed `napi.targets`","consequence":"Treated as absent, so the napi drift diagnostic is silently not produced. This is a deliberate 'lenient policy' in a comment, while matrix.rs hard-errors on the same input, so the two commands disagree.","fix":"Emit a warning diagnostic for a malformed napi.targets"}
{"file":"commands/release_artifacts.rs","line":257,"quote":"Err(_unavailable) => return Ok(Attempt::Transient { value: false, .. })","class":"SUSPECT","what_is_lost":"Why `gh attestation verify` could not run (gh missing, spawn error, timeout). The same CommandUnavailable collapse is in policy.rs:217 and at github.rs:142/197, tag.rs:197, npm.rs:155, cargo.rs:84, pypi.rs:214/334.","consequence":"This does fail closed. Retries are exhausted into 'GitHub attestation verification failed', so a missing gh looks like a bad attestation. The cause is lost, not the failure.","fix":"Carry the Io or TimedOut cause in CommandUnavailable and include it in the final error"}
{"file":"apply.rs","line":556","quote":"ManifestFormat::from_path(path).ok().map(|fmt| fmt.ecosystem())  // also :715","class":"SUSPECT","what_is_lost":"Unrecognised manifest filename in a write target","consequence":"The ecosystem is not marked active, so its lockfile is not refreshed or staged (apply.rs:715 skips the lockfile dir). I could not verify that a non-manifest path can reach here, and planned writes probably always have a known format. If one did, the lockfile would silently go stale in the version commit.","fix":"Treat an unknown format as an internal-invariant error"}
